{"_id":"6a2ff54c2204ffbc59e5a614","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"sBKhhjfFTpbj7TQwVnX7F","description":"# Parquet\n\nParquet is a columnar file format optimized for analytical workloads. It stores data with type information, supports efficient compression, and reads much faster than CSV for large datasets. `pd.read_parquet()` requires the `pyarrow` or `fastparquet` library and is the preferred format for storing processed DataFrames on disk.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.read_parquet","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.read_parquet.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb87"},{"type":"video","title":"Reading Parquet Files in Python","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XFO5jdGsMek","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb88"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:51:24.050Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/sBKhhjfFTpbj7TQwVnX7F.md"}